## Environment and commands

All tooling runs through [Pixi](https://pixi.sh/latest/). The project environment is *not* on
`PATH`, so always prefix commands with `pixi run` — calling bare `ruff`, `mypy`, `pytest` or
`python` will use the wrong interpreter.

```bash
pixi install              # create/refresh the environment (run once after cloning)
pixi run app              # run the {% if application_type == 'Library' %}package entry point{% else %}application{% endif %}
pixi run ruff format      # format code
pixi run ruff check       # lint
pixi run mypy .           # type-check
pixi run pytest           # run tests
pixi run coverage run && pixi run coverage report   # tests with coverage
```

Add dependencies with [`pixi add`](https://pixi.sh/dev/reference/cli/pixi/add/) rather than by
hand-editing `pyproject.toml`, so the lock file stays consistent.

