## Architecture: MVVM

The application follows the MVVM pattern provided by `nova-mvvm`. Keep the layers separate:

- **Models** (`models/`) are Pydantic `BaseModel` classes. Declare fields with `Field(...)` and
  fill in `title`, `description` and `examples` — the GUI reads that metadata to build and
  document its inputs. Models hold data and validation rules only.
- **View models** (`view_models/`) own state transitions and business logic. Create bindings with
  `binding.new_bind(...)` in `__init__`, react to changes through `callback_after_update`, and
  push updates to the UI with `update_in_view(...)`. View models must not import UI modules.
- **Views** (`views/`) build the interface and bind to view-model fields by name. No business
  logic, no direct model mutation, no I/O in a view.
- Every new view model must be registered in `create_viewmodels()` in `mvvm_factory.py`.
{% if framework == 'Trame' %}
Views build on `nova-trame`: compose the components from `nova.trame` (`ThemedApp`,
`nova.trame.view.components`, `nova.trame.view.layouts`) instead of using raw Trame widgets, so
theming and layout stay consistent with other NOVA tools.
{% endif %}{% endif %}
